    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x+y)(x+z)(y+z)$\n\nSplit $2xyz$ into $xyz+xyz$, then group four terms at a time.",
      "worked": "Split $2xyz$ into $xyz+xyz$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2y+x^2z+xy^2+2xyz+xz^2+y^2z+yz^2&=x(xy+xz+y^2+yz)+z(xy+xz+y^2+yz)\\\\x^2y+x^2z+xy^2+2xyz+xz^2+y^2z+yz^2&=(x+z)\\bigl[x(y+z)+y(y+z)\\bigr]\\\\x^2y+x^2z+xy^2+2xyz+xz^2+y^2z+yz^2&=(x+y)(x+z)(y+z).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
